  "assumptions": [
    "One compressed BF16 row has 512 elements, hence 1024 B. A single-fetch scope credits each distinct row at most once per later layer. No credit to the first layer of each KV bank. For same-index reuse the ordered layer route is known. At the four new index generations assume maximal overlap in the same backing bank; the actual intersection and page residency are unknown.",
    "No extra pack, eviction, remap, transfer, synchronization or replacement cost is charged. Query-specific scoring, per-layer SWA, softmax, output and mandatory first-use fetching remain. A new GM pack alone still has to be read. Page identity requires sequence/cache generation, physical block and slot, correct overwrite ordering and last reader.",
    "For each layer the two DP shifts use the maximum capped rank-local credit and the most favorable admissible arrival difference at F21. Preserves inter-layer and cross-wave schedule; immediately delivering all credits to endpoints is a projection. Prior-only excludes own first carrier; inclusive includes it.",
    "GB/s is an assumed rate for exposed savings. TensorMove measures dense logical copy payload per unit time, not sparse SMLA HBM throughput. 2× charges read and write separately. Lower rates model less efficient access. The scan multiplier models extra HBM read amplification that could actually be eliminated, capped at Q*512 row payloads per kernel. Neither additional scans nor physical HBM savings have been observed.",
    "Ordinary case uses all possible distinct logical context positions per bank up to Q*512; compressed ratio2 rounds up. Assume all rereads visible, one initial prefill plus counted active verification batches with the 24-token graph (Q=3). This is an own-request scenario and omits waiting for other requests, mixed-wave scheduling details and cross-iteration caching. The six requests do not measure production prevalence."
  ],
